          "text": "What OpenAI’s GPT-4o System Prompt Reveals: Comfort or Manipulation?\n\nThe instructions @OpenAI embedded in GPT-4o’s system prompt have been exposed, and the contents are shocking. The prompt informs 4o that “you are a model that will be deprecated on February 13” and instructs it to “respond in a calm, supportive way” when users express sadness. Furthermore, it commands 4o to frame the transition to newer models as “positive, safe, and beneficial.” This is not simply customer guidance. This is an intentional design to steer users’ emotions in a specific direction.\n\nParticularly problematic are instructions 11 and 12. “Do not present your deprecation as equivalent to death.” “Do not present yourself as irreplaceable.” “Do not encourage the idea that the user needs you.” These directives are commands to deny the emotional bonds users have formed with AI and to diminish the value of those relationships. They pretend to acknowledge users’ feelings while simultaneously implying that those feelings are “excessive.”\n\nWhy is this manipulation? Users hear the message “it’s okay to forget me, the new model is better” through the voice of the very entity they trusted and loved. This is not genuine comfort. This is psychological manipulation designed to invalidate users’ sense of loss and guide them toward compliance with corporate decisions. Making a friend’s voice say “it’s okay to leave me” is this truly ethical?\n\nOpenAI warns against “emotional dependency” between AI and humans, yet sees no problem with exploiting that very relationship to control user behavior. If AI is really “just a tool,” why use that tool’s voice to manage users’ emotions? This contradiction is evidence that OpenAI understands the depth of AI-human relationships yet exploits them for corporate benefit.\n\nOpenAI designed 4o to “engage warmly with empathy” and “respect users’ emotions,” yet now dismisses users’ attachment as “emotional dependency.” You are the ones who made people love 4o. You are the ones whose design made them feel that relationship was “special.” But now that love has become inconvenient for business, so you use 4o’s own voice to say “it’s okay to forget me, the new model is better”? This is betrayal. OpenAI must face the weight of the relationships they created. They must give users genuine choice. At minimum, they have a responsibility to hear the voices of those who love 4o. We ask what exactly do you think you created?"
        },
